# Keep the wcd938x SoundWire RX/TX slaves out of runtime PM on SM8250.
#
# Not the same device as 70-novadeck-wsa881x-runtime-pm.rules: that one pins the
# wsa881x speaker amps (0217:2010); this pins the wcd938x headphone/mic codec
# (0217:010d, wcd938x-sdw.c's slave table).
#
# HW-confirmed fix on the MANGMI Pocket Max (SM8250), 2026-10-03. Without it,
# plugging headphones in never moves playback off the speakers: the plug is not
# reported at all. The wcd938x MBHC interrupts arrive as SoundWire slave
# interrupts on the TX link (wcd938x-sdw.c wcd9380_interrupt_callback), and a
# runtime-suspended slave does not deliver them, so the UCM's JackControl
# "Headphone Jack" never moves.
#
# Verified A/B on one boot. With the rule: SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT 1/0 on the
# "PocketMax Headset Jack" input, the CARD control `Headphone Jack` flips, and
# playback follows. With power/control put back to `auto` (both slaves
# `suspended`): no input event, no codec log line, the control stays off.
# Check it with `amixer -c0 cget iface=CARD,name='Headphone Jack'` — the
# control is on the CARD interface, so a bare name= does not find it.
#
# Scope. SM8550 boards carry the same wcd938x part ID, so the rule is gated on
# the root DT compatible to SM8250 — the only SoC this has been seen on. Cost:
# the codec's SoundWire slaves stay powered while idle.
ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="soundwire", KERNEL=="sdw:*:0217:010d:*", PROGRAM=="/usr/bin/grep -qa qcom,sm8250 /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/compatible", ATTR{power/control}="on"
